    Home appliances — washing machines, refrigerators, air conditioners, microwaves, water heaters — sit differently from small electronics. They are heavier, they often carry refrigerant or oil, and after 8-10 years of use their resale value is usually limited. This page covers what appliances get accepted, how bulky-item transport is planned, and what happens to refrigerant-carrying units before the metal, plastic and copper are separated for recovery.
  </p>

